WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.640
Whether you're a devoted Stranger Things fan
looking for a refresher, or a casual fan looking

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.690
for a point of reference, we're digging into
the history of Hawkins, Indiana's association

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:13.190
with the Upside Down, from the first experiments
conducted at Hawkins Lab to the Battle of

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.620
Starcourt and beyond.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.780
The chain of events that kicked things off
actually began more than a decade before the

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.020
series itself.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:25.950
In 1969, Dr. Martin Brenner arrives at Hawkins
National Laboratory to oversee the MKUltra

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:31.230
program, which dosed test subjects with hallucinogenic
drugs in an effort to manifest superhuman

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.000
abilities.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.880
"She was part of some study in college."

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.120
"MKUltra."

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:37.800
"Yeah, that's the one."

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:43.180
It's through this new screening process that
he eventually meets Terry Ives, who took part

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:47.220
in MKUltra trials at Hawkins in the early
1970s.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.740
Though she apparently didn't know it at the
time, Terry was pregnant when the trials began.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:55.780
When he discovers this, Dr. Brenner hatches
a plan to take control of Terry's eventual

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.640
baby at all costs.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:03.120
After undergoing MKUltra trials that included
some time in a sensory deprivation tank, Terry

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.000
Ives gives birth to a daughter.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:09.680
She would've named her baby girl Jane, but
Brenner immediately orchestrates a coverup,

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:13.270
claiming that Terry had actually miscarried
before she was eventually discharged from

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.260
the trials.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.800
Terry is convinced that she had a baby, and
files lawsuits in an attempt to get information,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.260
but her efforts fail.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:25.980
Around 1974, Terry attempts to infiltrate
Hawkins Lab and steal her baby back, but she's

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:26.880
apprehended.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.160
In an effort to keep her baby secret, Brenner
subjects her to intense electro-convulsive

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.909
therapy before releasing her back to her sister
in a vegetative state.

00:01:34.909 --> 00:01:39.459
For the rest of her life Terry can only repeat
the sequence of events leading up to her capture

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.740
on an endless loop.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.600
"Breathe.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.320
Sunflower.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.500
Rainbow.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.740
Four fifty.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.240
Breathe."

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:54.099
With the coverup seemingly secure, Brenner
continues to groom Terry's daughter, who he

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:58.700
dubs Eleven, by forming a father-daughter
bond with her and urging her to call him "Papa."

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:04.219
At some point in the 1970s, Eight manages
to escape and flee to Chicago, where she forms

00:02:04.219 --> 00:02:09.250
a chosen family of misfits and sets out to
exact vengeance on anyone tied to the MKUltra

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:10.240
program.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.600
As the '70s turn into the '80s, Brenner continues
frequent testing of Eleven's abilities, which

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.630
ultimately include both telekinesis and telepathy.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:23.590
He starts small, asking her to use her mind
to crush a Coca-Cola can, but then attempts

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.720
to push her further by asking her to use the
same ability on a living cat.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:32.700
When she refuses, he attempts to confine her
to a locked cell, and while resisting, Eleven

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.230
kills two guards with her mind, inadvertently
granting Brenner a successful test of her

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.520
telekinesis on living tissue.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:44.760
Next come more advanced tests of her telepathy,
which begin by asking Eleven to listen to

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.960
the thoughts of a man elsewhere in the lab.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.880
She's able to not only hear him, but to broadcast
what he's saying over the lab loudspeakers.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:56.140
Brenner then pushes further, putting Eleven
in a sensory deprivation tank to test the

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:58.040
limits of her eavesdropping ability.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.620
When she's pushed even further, she makes
contact with a strange monster, apparently

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:03.970
from another world.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:06.860
Brenner, intrigued by this, wants to dig deeper.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:13.160
On November 6, 1983, Eleven is tasked with
making contact with the monster again.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:17.620
The mission goes wrong, and Eleven accidentally
opens a gate between dimensions, allowing

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:22.140
the creature to break loose and kill scientists
within Hawkins Lab before escaping.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.819
In the chaos, Eleven also manages to flee
the lab, triggering a wide search for her

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:31.380
during which government agents are constantly
covering their tracks, on Brenner's orders.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:36.200
The monster, later dubbed the Demogorgon,
flees into the woods around Hawkins, and ultimately

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.950
abducts a young boy, Will Byers, who's on
his way home after a game of Dungeons &amp; Dragons

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.220
with his friends Mike Wheeler, Dustin Henderson,
and Lucas Sinclair.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.440
"It was a seven."

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.220
"Huh?"

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:47.230
"The roll.

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:48.520
It was a seven.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.280
The Demogorgon.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:51.040
It got me."

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:55.080
The Hawkins community begins an intensive
search for Will, but it is ultimately his

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.060
mother, Joyce, who discovers that he's in
another dimension.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:03.340
During the search, another local, Barb Holland,
is abducted by the Demogorgon during a party.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:07.900
Will and Barb are both taken to the Demogorgon's
home dimension, a dark place that the Hawkins

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.130
kids will later dub "The Upside Down."

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:14.090
Meanwhile, the hunt for Eleven continues,
as government agents ruthlessly search for

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:18.680
her, killing witnesses to tie up loose ends,
including the kindly owner of a local diner

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:19.680
who gave her food.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:24.680
The killing in the diner, combined with Will
Byers' disappearance, leads police chief Jim

00:04:24.689 --> 00:04:28.099
Hopper to begin investigating these strange
things in earnest.

00:04:28.099 --> 00:04:32.490
Eleven, still on the run, meets up with Mike,
Dustin, and Lucas, and ultimately convinces

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:34.200
them that she can help find Will.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:38.380
Brenner and his government cronies engineer
a dramatic cover-up, faking Will's death by

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.960
planting a dummy body in a local reservoir.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.740
Everyone believes it's really Will except
for Joyce and Eleven.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:49.240
Eleven succeeds in convincing Mike by using
her powers to project his voice from the Upside

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:53.919
Down, while Hopper follows Joyce's suspicion
to the morgue and discovers the body is full

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:54.740
of cotton.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.260
He decides to infiltrate the Hawkins Lab to
find out what's really going on, and briefly

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:03.040
glimpses the gate before he's knocked unconscious
and returned to his home under government

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.040
surveillance.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.360
"You were right."

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:11.360
Hopper researches the lab and finds evidence
of Terry Ives and the MKUltra trials.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.590
He and Joyce travel to meet Terry and are
told by her sister Becky that Terry always

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.440
believed she had a secret daughter.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:22.120
Meanwhile, Barb's friend Nancy, who is also
Mike's sister, and Will's brother Jonathan

00:05:22.129 --> 00:05:27.009
have come to believe that a monster is responsible
for Barb's disappearance, and Nancy briefly

00:05:27.009 --> 00:05:29.240
enters the Upside Down while searching for
it.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:34.060
In an effort to amplify her eavesdropping
powers, the boys build a sensory deprivation

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.100
tank for Eleven at Hawkins Middle School.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:41.240
She discovers Barb died, but Will is alive,
being pursued by the Demogorgon as it hops

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.040
dimensions.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:46.000
Joyce and Hopper return to Hawkins Lab to
confront Brenner, who reveals that he and

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.500
his men are unable to control the Demogorgon.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:53.539
Meanwhile, Nancy and Jonathan return to the
Byers house and set traps for the Demogorgon,

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.820
where Joyce has repeatedly seen both it and
Will in the walls.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:00.540
With the help of Nancy's boyfriend Steve they
fight it, but it flees.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:05.059
In the Upside Down, Joyce and Hopper locate
Will, now pinned down and intertwined with

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:06.680
a large alien tendril.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:10.240
They free him, and Hopper performs CPR until
he's breathing again.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.620
They return to Hawkins.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:16.710
At the school, Brenner and his agents converge
on Eleven when the Demogorgon suddenly appears.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:20.590
Eleven confronts it directly and uses her
power to apparently disintegrate it, but in

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:22.900
the process she herself vanishes.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:28.140
A month after the Demogorgon is defeated,
there are still echoes of what came before.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:32.720
Brenner was attacked by the Demogorgon, and
then seemed to disappear from Hawkins as the

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.380
lab came under new management.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:38.659
Mike misses Eleven, and begins regular attempts
to make contact with her on his radio.

00:06:38.659 --> 00:06:43.219
Hopper, who received some mysterious information
from someone in a car at the end of the first

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:47.580
season, begins leaving food out in the woods
for Eleven to find, hoping to lure her back.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:51.280
We later learn that Eleven's efforts sent
her into the Upside Down.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:56.419
At some point in November of 1983, she broke
free, hiding in the woods before being secretly

00:06:56.419 --> 00:06:57.809
taken in by Hopper.

00:06:57.809 --> 00:07:02.809
Months later, in June of 1984, Russian scientists
attempt to use a machine called the Key to

00:07:02.809 --> 00:07:04.330
access the Upside Down.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:09.340
They fail, and new plans are made to try to
access the dark dimension from another location

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:12.480
via covert land purchases in Hawkins, Indiana.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.300
In October of 1984, there's more trouble brewing.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:20.780
Eleven is beginning to grow restless, using
her powers to explore the possibility of contacting

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:21.780
Mike again.

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:26.600
Out in Hawkins proper, Hopper is bothered
by a seemingly simple new problem: Complaints

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:30.849
of crop deterioration around the area, including
the local pumpkin patch.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:35.020
Meanwhile, Nancy and Jonathan learn that Barb's
parents have convinced a private investigator

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:37.240
to look into their daughter's disappearance.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:40.620
The biggest problem, however, is brewing within
Will Byers.

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:45.180
Ever since he came back from the Upside Down,
he's been experiencing strange symptoms connected

00:07:45.189 --> 00:07:50.149
to it, including visions of a massive, spider-like
creature towering over the horizon.

00:07:50.149 --> 00:07:54.800
Finally, on Halloween night, Will has another
vision and tells Mike that he's been seeing

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:55.600
things.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:59.460
After a night spent trick-or-treating, Dustin
comes across a strange lizard-like creature

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:02.440
from the Upside Down in the trash can behind
his house.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:08.260
Dustin names the creature D'Artagnan or "Dart"
for short, and while it's initially small

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:13.119
enough to fit into a terrarium, it soon grows
dramatically until it's the size of a dog.

00:08:13.119 --> 00:08:16.860
Soon, the gang comes to discover there are
more of them, and that they've invaded the

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:21.279
town through new entrances to the Upside Down
in tunnels caused by the continued spread

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:23.180
of that dimension's influence.

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:27.880
As Will Byers opens up to his mother about
his visions, which ultimately turn into seizures,

00:08:27.889 --> 00:08:32.340
he begins scribbling out drawings to explain
his psychic and physical links to a new creature

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:34.520
that the kids call the Mind Flayer.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:39.080
These drawings form a map that corresponds
to the dead crops Hopper's been seeing.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.120
"The Eno River.

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:42.920
And there it is.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.120
That's the Eno, don't you see it?"

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:49.760
When he investigates these things directly,
he falls into the tunnels, revealing just

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.960
how far the contamination has spread.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:56.080
Meanwhile, Eleven has begun digging through
Hopper's old evidence files for information

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:57.140
about her mother.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:01.300
She reconnects with Terry through a psychic
link, uncovering Terry's failed attempt to

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:02.220
save her baby.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:06.000
"Jane."

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.040
"Mama?"

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:16.640
Having recognized her mother, Eleven hitch-hikes
to the Ives home, convincing Becky to let

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:17.620
her see Terry.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:21.900
As she probes her mother's mind, Eleven is
shown a vision of a little girl she used to

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:26.340
play with in the lab, and with the help of
old photos Becky provides her, she heads for

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:27.240
Chicago.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:32.020
There, Eleven meets Kali, who's been in hiding
after her time in the lab for years, using

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:36.220
her perception-altering powers to survive
while nurturing a group of misfits.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:40.860
Kali helps Eleven to realize the full extent
of her gifts, and helps her to feel as though

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:42.420
she isn't alone in the world.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:46.760
She also lets Eleven in on her mission: Finding
and killing those who were responsible for

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.740
ripping them from their families and experimenting
on them.

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:54.550
At first, Eleven is eager to exact vengeance
on bad people who harmed her and her mother,

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:58.710
but when she realizes Kali is asking her to
purposefully and mercilessly kill people in

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:03.970
cold blood, she ultimately declines to be
part of it, and after seeing a vision of Mike

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:08.580
and Hopper in danger in Hawkins as a result
of the escalating activity of the Mind Flayer,

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.000
she decides to go home.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:14.900
Will's increasing physical deterioration at
the hands of the Mind Flayer, coupled with

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:18.800
the violence of the Demodogs, all suggest
some sort of hive mind is at work.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:23.360
This all leads to a showdown in Hawkins Lab
in which numerous people, including Joyce's

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:25.160
boyfriend Bob, are killed.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:29.780
Their struggle is helped along by the return
of Eleven, and a plan is hatched: To keep

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:34.240
the Mind Flayer blind and distracted, Joyce,
Jonathan, and Nancy will take a sedated Will

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:38.260
to Hopper's cabin and try to use intense heat
to drive the Flayer out.

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:42.720
Meanwhile Mike, Dustin, Lucas, Steve, and
their new friend Max will set fire to the

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.200
tunnels as a distraction.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:48.080
Eleven and Hopper will sneak back into the
lab, where Eleven will use her powers to close

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:51.280
the gate she inadvertently opened a year earlier.

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:53.860
The plan ultimately works.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:58.170
The Mind Flayer is forced out of Will, Eleven
closes the gate, and the kids all escape the

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:02.020
tunnels alive, with the threats from the Upside
Down apparently at an end.

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:06.240
Due to evidence Jonathan and Nancy gathered
throughout the season, Hawkins Lab is shut

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:09.920
down after a public outcry, and Barb is given
a proper funeral.

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:14.180
Hopper meets with the lab's new director,
Sam Owens, who grants him legal custody of

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:18.800
Eleven through a forged birth certificate,
cementing their father-daughter relationship.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:23.740
As the season ends in December of 1984, all
the kids get together for the annual Snow

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:28.460
Ball dance, during which Eleven and Mike finally
become a couple, and Max and Lucas also get

00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:29.160
together.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:33.620
As they celebrate, it's revealed that the
Mind Flayer is still very much alive, and

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:37.760
is watching them all from the Upside Down,
signaling that it's not done with its attempt

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.460
to conquer just yet.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:44.480
In the early months of 1985, Russian scientists
make some illicit land deals with Hawkins'

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:45.960
Mayor Larry Kline.

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:51.020
After buying property, they move into a clandestine
facility beneath the Starcourt Mall and construct

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:54.990
a new version of the key, which marks the
beginning of a new connection between our

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:56.980
world and the Upside Down.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:03.880
On June 28, 1984, a blackout hits Hawkins
and rats in the area begin flocking to the

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:07.660
old Brimborn Steelworks on the edge of town
for unknown reasons.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:12.340
This escalates when Billy Hargrove, Max's
older stepbrother, crashes his car near the

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:14.880
Steelworks on the night of June 29.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:19.240
In a daze, Billy is swept into the Steelworks
and possessed by the Mind Flayer.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:24.060
With the gate slowly reopening, the Mind Flayer
has found a way to re-establish its hivemind

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:28.790
in Hawkins, breaking down the rats' bodies
and using them as raw material to build itself

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:30.620
a horrifying new form.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:35.400
Meanwhile on a hilltop outside of town, Dustin
sets up a radio antenna he built while at

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:39.460
summer camp in an effort to communicate with
his long-distance girlfriend, Susie.

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:43.700
He's unable to reach her, but he does pick
up a strange message in Russian, which he

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:46.870
records and takes to Steve, who now works
at the local mall.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:47.840
"Pleasure to meet you.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:49.360
Uh, is he here?"

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:50.600
"Is who here?"

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:54.940
"Henderson! Henderson!

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:55.940
He's back!"

00:12:56.220 --> 00:13:00.280
Steve's coworker at the Scoops Ahoy ice cream
shop, Robin, believes she can decipher the

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:02.340
code with the help of a Russian dictionary.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:07.440
The now-possessed Billy abducts his co-worker
at the local pool, Heather, and exposes her

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:09.540
to the Mind Flayer's possession as well.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:14.620
As part of a sleepover prank, Eleven eavesdrops
on Billy's mind and suspects something is

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:15.460
amiss.

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:20.080
Eleven and Max begin to investigate, while
Jonathan and Nancy investigate the rats.

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:25.060
Meanwhile, Joyce alerts Hopper to some strange
magnetic activity she's noticed around town,

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:26.960
and asks him to take her back to the Lab.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:36.060
"You stand me up, no phone call, no apology,
because you had to go to Scott Clark's house?"

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:37.200
"Yeah."

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:41.640
They begin investigating while Robin, Steve,
and Dustin realize that the Russian message

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:44.240
is a code related to the Starcourt Mall itself.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:48.800
Joyce and Hopper intimidate Kline, who comes
clean about his ties to secret land purchases

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:49.800
around town.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:54.480
They visit one of the properties, a farm house,
and discover Russians at work in the basement,

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:59.120
confirming a Soviet presence in town even
as the Scoops Troop at the mall is also uncovering

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:00.410
similar details.

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:04.180
Meanwhile, Will tells his friends that he
can sense the Mind Flayer's presence, and

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:06.260
they suspect that Billy has been taken over.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:10.860
The kids trap Billy in the sauna at the pool,
confirming the presence of the Mind Flayer

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:14.180
and its hivemind, which has now infected the
residents of Hawkins.

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:18.960
As the kids try to figure out what to do about
the Mind Flayer, Dustin, Robin, Steve, and

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:23.180
Lucas' little sister Erica have accidentally
infiltrated a Russian facility beneath the

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:23.980
mall.

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:28.400
Joyce and Hopper manage to capture Alexei,
a Russian scientist, and take him to Murray

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:30.480
Bauman to get him to translate.

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:34.980
After being bribed with a Slurpee, Alexei
explains the entire plot to use the key to

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:39.370
open the gate to the Upside Down again in
Hawkins, and Hopper places a call to Owens

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:41.080
to ask the government to intervene.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:42.380
"Dude.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:44.360
You did it!

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.060
You won a fight!"

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:50.800
Back in Hawkins, the Mind Flayer is now aware
that the kids are onto it, and begins sending

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:53.800
possessed people to attempt to kill or convert
them.

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:58.490
Robin and Steve are captured in the facility
and Erica and Dustin hide, and Eleven goes

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:03.120
into the Void, and discovers the Mind Flayer,
who reveals its plan to convert all of Hawkins

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:06.320
to its cause, growing until it breaks out
of the Steelworks.

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:13.180
On the night of July 4, 1985, all of the major
players in Hawkins converge on Starcourt Mall.The

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:17.780
kids head there after Eleven sees Dustin in
the Void and Dustin, Erica, Steve, and Robin

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:20.120
all manage to escape the underground facility.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:25.020
The Mind Flayer pursues them, hoping to possess
or destroy Eleven once and for all, while

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:29.200
Joyce and Hopper head into the facility to
destroy the key and close the gate once again.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:33.640
A battle ensues, with the kids distracting
the Mind Flayer by throwing fireworks at it.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:37.640
Down in the Soviet facility, the other team
gets a little help from Dustin's girlfriend

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:42.390
Suzie, who provides Planck's Constant via
the radio to help them gain access after singing

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.500
the theme to The Neverending Story.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:48.620
Billy appears to stop Eleven, but when she
uses memories of his childhood to get through

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:53.040
to him, Billy remembers who he really is and
sacrifices himself to save her.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:58.100
At the same time, Hopper battles the Terminator-like
Grigori near the key, then tells Joyce to

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.520
shut the machine down.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:04.540
The key explodes, the Gate closes, the Mind
Flayer is destroyed, and Hopper is apparently

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:05.870
killed in the blast.

00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:09.380
Outside, Sam Owens and a squadron of government
agents arrive.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:14.960
In October of 1985, three months after the
battle of Starcourt, the Byers family, now

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:19.120
including Eleven as Joyce's adopted daughter,
plan to move away from Hawkins.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:23.540
Mayor Kline has been arrested, the Russian
plot discovered, and Hawkins has become something

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.840
of a conspiracy theorist's dream town.

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:30.280
The biggest change of all, though, seems to
be that Eleven no longer has her powers, having

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:32.580
been drained by her battle with the Mind Flayer.

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:36.980
She and Mike make a pact to see each other
again for the holidays, and the Byers drive

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:41.000
away, after Eleven reads a speech about what
Hopper wanted for her future.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:46.600
At an unknown date sometime later, at a facility
in Kamchatka, Russia, soldiers are shown feeding

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:49.260
an unnamed man to a captive Demogorgon.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:52.700
Before they do, though, they mention "The
American" in another cell.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:57.120
The American is not named, but it's implied
that it could be Jim Hopper, still alive.

